<details><summary>How this page works</summary>

- Rendered from GitHub and `magus queue ls` after every queue run and on every label, review or auto-merge event; edits here do not survive.
- Rows rank by how near each is to merging: validating, queued in queue order, can join. Kicked-back rows sit below, unranked.
- A box runs when someone with write access checks it; any other check is ignored and the page is rendered again.
- Queue and Requeue enable auto-merge as the queue app; Rerun reruns the failed jobs; Run the queue now starts a validation run on `main` unless one is waiting.
- Past it counts merges whose `merge-queue` status was not success.
- Render it yourself: `magus buzz hack/ci/pull-requests.buzz -- dashboard --all --base main --preview --out dashboard.md`

</details>

